WEBVTT

00:00:27.913 --> 00:00:30.746
but that's only because
we're so used to doing it.

00:00:30.871 --> 00:00:33.079
It turns out this is actually
a complex problem

00:00:33.121 --> 00:00:37.204
that requires sophisticated coordination
inside your brain.

00:00:37.246 --> 00:00:39.746
That's because to create
these new, weird images,

00:00:39.746 --> 00:00:43.954
your brain takes familiar pieces
and assembles them in new ways,

00:00:43.996 --> 00:00:47.162
like a collage made
from fragments of photos.

00:00:47.704 --> 00:00:51.204
The brain has to juggle a sea
of thousands of electrical signals

00:00:51.246 --> 00:00:55.621
getting them all to their destination
at precisely the right time.

00:00:56.496 --> 00:00:57.912
When you look at an object,

00:00:57.954 --> 00:01:01.454
thousands of neurons
in your posterior cortex fire.